n","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:7","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(3) The combining of any two or more lots, tracts, or parcels of property for any purpose; or","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"f6bfa92a-e7de-5f96-8616-420c084a71a6"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"32cd2cc5df39049a56a31e65292c58437ebed5fa8cc16f304d0828c0b349f3e1","heading":null,"ordinal":8,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:8","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(4) The preparation of land for any of the above purposes; or","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"8e6bc75a-0641-5cea-838e-8b39ebe84b29"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"117bd1c4238534e289933ef2a1eadfe4d75d3b4998f8736aa3c7b44d6f071f89","heading":null,"ordinal":9,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:9","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(5) The clearing of trees and vegetation and/or excavation or earthwork on a tract or parcel of land.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"26d1da90-706e-5046-9737-3e8e1d679e5d"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"22f1b92503d6b673f558079c371bbcdaaff5599d91986deec4de0fa260b98c88","heading":null,"ordinal":10,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:10","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“GIS-based stream buffer shapefiles for the City of Topeka” means a shapefile developed using hydraulic modeling results and site-specific characteristics to determine the magnitude of stream setback limits using a process that evaluates the overall risk along the stream, direction of flow, and minimum bank offset. The science-based stream buffer highlights areas where bank failure is more likely to occur and where additional setback measures are needed to protect the integrity of the stream channel. This file shall be used to determine the stream buffer width for the outer area.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"c061797b-8f14-5139-b6e7-0ed1dea68a8e"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"d3a8bf314df7fd6756b449d4db0e2e9f6a0b8daa1a323b8022b411316b75214d","heading":null,"ordinal":11,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:11","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Levee” means a manmade structure to control, divert, and contain stormwater runoff and flood flows.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"ff3e6967-79d9-5a59-986c-d3fc897b1a64"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"181659c547732b2cbfffdeb56d649786cf17653d6286d599df2e77f1aa950204","heading":null,"ordinal":12,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:12","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Native vegetation” means vegetation comprised of plant species that are indigenous to the area in question.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"e27c258b-3e45-53a8-b2d8-b6ff36371670"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"b9de78e587c030e3b46cb6ce9c32400a5aeb229e06b7f2d437cc6326865e1eb5","heading":null,"ordinal":13,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:13","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Nonpoint source pollution” means pollution which is generated by various land use activities rather than from an identifiable or discrete source and is conveyed to waterways through natural processes such as rainfall, storm runoff, or groundwater seepage rather than direct discharge.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"9962a242-c75b-5e5b-b526-b3db75ea7051"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"9c9bdc2255785c1b32e4f871bf7974881854309a3187ff47d038308a0bdca2f2","heading":null,"ordinal":14,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:14","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Pollution” means any contamination or alteration of the physical, chemical, or biological properties of any waters that will render the waters harmful or detrimental to domestic, commercial, industrial, agricultural, recreational, or other legitimate beneficial uses, livestock, wild animals, birds, fish or other aquatic life.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"81729ed9-d617-51e6-be03-47d409ba1aa6"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"d66fc017471f13be3c76eca2c77386ba87c809335152d1e0a0d21a14ead65a97","heading":null,"ordinal":15,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:15","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Streams” means perennial and intermittent watercourses identified through site inspection, drainage study, or United States Geological Survey (USGS) maps and further defined and categorized as follows:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"986b62e3-1775-59c9-b49a-3d918c14399c"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"e2215f741bf3690c155a02b5fbb22c64854802cd518ac0a971f70c7586d2112f","heading":null,"ordinal":16,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:16","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(1) “Type I streams” are defined as perennial streams shown as solid blue lines on a United States Geological Survey seven-and-one-half-minute series topographical map.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1c53e7c0-4886-5d23-bde5-824229d76ca7"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"14ed0ddd15a90424245fdcde6b2d4b8e8d65551329cf257e59e1315b8f7172a1","heading":null,"ordinal":17,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:17","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(2) “Type II streams” are defined as intermittent streams shown as dashed blue lines on a United States Geological Survey seven-and-one-half-minute series topographical map.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"6552d811-8edf-50ec-bbab-28ed4bfb7e18"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"a67337259a08f9b46dbe54e71fa8b4106db494d35edb0974f0661885e8fcee09","heading":null,"ordinal":18,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:18","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"(3) “Type III streams” are defined as waterways or dry channels that have a contributing drainage area of 40 acres or greater.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"a83e96c8-d7c2-526f-bb8a-219a7d8237d9"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"a2d678d9ede80ab677793017a28bee19bf687883619a89fe0965c54697f2c1d1","heading":null,"ordinal":19,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:17.10.020:block:19","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","text":"“Water pollution hazard” means a land use or activity that causes a relatively high risk of potential water pollution.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"fc7c3b64-cdaa-584f-b40a-eda2431050e3"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"17.10.020","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/17.10.020","content_hash":"6b21eda471151dc7e4edce295e081bbb7c1